# Called by Name (side quest, docs/story/side_quests.md): Big Tobar's son Nelu went into the trees after his dead
# mother's voice. The voices are will-o'-wisps in the gorge under Tser Falls, feeding on grief and speaking with the
# voices of the dead; Nelu is alive on a ledge, and they've been calling his father in Nelu's voice. At the falls
# after dark they call the party too, each by someone they lost. Reached from Zora's rumour (tser_camp:zora_road) or
# Tobar himself (tser_camp:tobar). Every line here is unvoiced for now; Nelu is a new speaker.

~ asks
quest called_by_name asked
# Three days from now Nelu answers the voices (data/quests/called_by_name.json closes: answered; Failure Plan T1).
if not flag.nelu_asked_at
set nelu_asked_at = now
endif
Big Tobar: You heard. Zora counts everything, even the things you'd rather she didn't.
Big Tobar: Three nights ago my boy Nelu was sitting up by the fire, and he stood up and said: that's Mama. And he walked off toward the falls track. His mother's been in the ground six years.
Big Tobar [sad]: I went after him. Halfway to the falls I heard him. "Da. Da, I'm down here. Da, come down." Out of the gorge, out of the dark. I'd have gone over the edge after him if Petru hadn't sat on me.
Big Tobar: Nobody here will go to the falls at night. I'm not asking anybody here. I'm asking you.
* [Insight DC 12] (Does he think the boy is alive?) -> hope | no_read
* We'll go to the falls after dark. -> agree
* Not yet. -> END

~ hope
Narrator: He doesn't. Not really. He's asking you to bring something back so there's something to bury, and he hates himself for it.
-> agree

~ no_read
Narrator: A big man holding a spoke so tightly it's bending.
-> agree

~ agree
Big Tobar: Whatever calls you, don't answer it. Whoever it sounds like. Especially then. I said that to strangers on the road for twenty years, and I never once thought to say it to my own son.
Big Tobar [sad]: Three days he's been down there without a crust of bread. Give it three more and the cold, or his mother's voice, will finish what the hunger started.
-> END

# --- Tobar afterwards (tser_camp:tobar jumps here) ---

~ tobar
if flag.nelu_home
-> tobar_after
endif
if quest.called_by_name == answered
Big Tobar [sad]: He used to hold the iron tire while I drove the spokes home, steady as an oak. Now I set two wedges where his hands ought to be, and the wheel still wobbles.
Big Tobar: A man can mend a split rim or a cracked axle before the kettle boils. There isn't a tool in my chest for this.
-> END
endif
if flag.nelu_saved
-> tobar_return
endif
Big Tobar: The falls. After dark. Don't answer.
-> END

~ tobar_return
set nelu_home
quest called_by_name home
Narrator: Nelu comes into the firelight a step behind you, filthy, shaking, alive. Big Tobar drops the wheel he's holding on his own foot and doesn't notice.
Big Tobar: Nelu. Nelu. You great idiot. You great, beautiful idiot.
Nelu: It was her voice, Da. It knew how she said my name.
Big Tobar: I know, boy. I know. It used yours on me.
Big Tobar: I've a little money put by for his wedding. He can earn it again. And this, off a dead archer on the road last winter; it holds more arrows than a quiver should, and I can't shoot to save my life.
gold +100
give efficient_quiver
approve thistle +2 godrick_pendlebrook +2 kip_smudgewick +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You brought Big Tobar's son home from the falls
-> END

~ tobar_after
Big Tobar: Nelu sits with his back to the falls now, and sings over anything that calls. Badly. It works.
-> END

# --- Nelu among the Vallaki Vistani when the pool camp has turned on the party (Side Quest Failure Plan, T1) ---
# Tobar is hidden with the rest of the camp, so nobody at the pool can take the boy home: he waits at the lake camp outside
# Vallaki's west gate (data/locations/vallaki_vistani_camp.json) and the quest closes there, without Tobar's money or quiver.

~ nelu_away
if quest.called_by_name == no_fire
Nelu [weary]: I sit with my back to the lake now, because water sounds the same everywhere once the sun goes down.
Nelu: I do not ask after the pool camp anymore, and if anything calls my name from the reeds, I sing over it until it gives up.
-> END
endif
quest called_by_name no_fire
Narrator: A woman by the lake fire puts a bowl of hot mutton broth into Nelu's hands and pulls a dry wool blanket around his thin shoulders.
Nelu [weary]: They gave me bread and fat, and a coat that smells like somebody else's horse, and they told me the road back to the pool is shut.
Nelu [sad]: Nobody here says why I cannot go home. Have you seen my Da on the road, or is he only looking for me in the wrong part of the trees?
Narrator: The mist off the lake is cold on your face, and the fire snaps in the quiet while the boy waits for an answer you do not have.
Nelu [sad]: That is all right. You pulled me off the wet rock when the water was loud, and that was work enough for one week.
Nelu: When the mist comes up from the water tonight, I am going to sing every song I know until the dark has no room left to talk.
-> END

# --- At the falls after dark (prop gorge_voices) ---

~ falls
if quest.called_by_name == answered
if night
Narrator: Pale lights drift through the mist beneath the falls, murmuring in stolen voices that echo off the wet rock.
Narrator: A new glow hangs lower than the rest, calling for its Da in a thin, shivering boy's voice.
else
Narrator: Below, the falls thunder into cold spray. Partway down the slick gorge wall, a narrow shelf of black stone sits washed clean and empty.
endif
-> END
endif
if flag.wisps_beaten
-> ledge
endif
if flag.nelu_saved
-> ledge
endif
if not night
-> falls_day
endif
quest called_by_name voices
Narrator: Down in the gorge there are lights: small, pale, drifting like lanterns carried by people who are taking their time. Under the roar of the water, somebody is calling.
Narrator: Then they're calling you. Each of you. By name.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Sir Pellam? That's... that's his voice. "Godrick, lad. Bring the sword down here. I'll do it properly this time."
endif
if name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Sorrel. It's Sorrel, telling me to stop slouching. He's been dead two years. He'd never come back just for that. He would, actually.
endif
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: That's my grandda. He's saying come on, lass, it's not far. It's no' him. It's no' him. I know it's no' him.
endif
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Pip? Pip, sweetheart, what are you... No. No, she's home. She's home and she's safe and that is not my daughter.
endif
if name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: It's praying, in the voice of the old sister who taught me. It doesn't know the words. It's just making the shapes.
endif
if name:ratatoille
interject name:ratatoille: Maman, calling me out of the kitchen. She never once called me out of the kitchen. She needed me in it.
endif
Narrator: And under all of it, a boy's voice, hoarse from shouting: Da. Da, come down.
check Wisdom DC 14 -> steady | lured

~ steady
Narrator: You hold. Whatever the voices are, they've noticed you're not coming down to them, and they're coming up.
combat falls_wisps

~ lured
set wisps_lured
Narrator: Someone takes a step toward the edge, and then another, and the voice in their ear is so glad. By the time the rest of you have hold of them, the lights are already on the ledge with you.
combat falls_wisps

# --- After the lights are out (the same prop) ---

~ ledge
if flag.nelu_saved
Narrator: The gorge is dark and loud and empty. Nothing down there knows your name.
-> END
endif
Narrator: The lights are gone. Under the roar of the water there's still one voice, hoarse and very real: "Da? Is somebody there? I can't climb it. I've tried."
* [Athletics DC 13] (Rope off a pine and go down for him.) -> climb | climb_fail
* [knows:misty_step] (Step down to his ledge and back with him.) -> carried
* [knows:spider_climb] (Walk down the rock with Spider Climb.) -> carried
* Shout that you'll be back. -> END

~ climb_fail
time +30
Narrator: The rock is slick with spray and the rope burns through your hands. You come back up empty and bleeding, and the boy's voice says: it's all right. It's all right. Try again.
-> END

~ climb
-> carried

~ carried
set nelu_saved
quest called_by_name nelu_found
Narrator: He's on a shelf of wet rock no wider than a cart, twenty feet down, soaked and shaking and three days hungry, with his knees pulled up and his hands over his ears.
Nelu: Is it you? Really you? They used everybody's voice. They used my Da's.
Nelu: Get me home. Please. And don't let anything say my name on the way.
-> END

# --- By day: the same ledge, no lights, and a way down that doesn't need the fight (NPC plan batch 2) ---

~ falls_day
Narrator: Below the lip of the gorge, Tser Falls roars down through wet black rock into a pale churning mist.
Narrator: Twenty feet down, a thin boy lies curled on a shelf no wider than a cart, his hands pressed tight over his ears.
Narrator: No lights drift in the grey daylight, only cold spray, and at the crunch of your boots he looks up.
-> falls_day_menu

~ falls_day_menu
* [Athletics DC 13] (Rope off a pine and go down for him.) -> climb_day | climb_fail
* [Survival DC 12] (Read the rock for a way down.) -> climb_survival | climb_fail
* [knows:misty_step] (Step down to his ledge and back with him.) -> spell_day
* [knows:spider_climb] (Walk down the rock with Spider Climb.) -> spell_day
* (Call down to him.) -> nelu_day_hail
* (Come back after dark.) -> END

~ nelu_day_hail
Narrator: He squints up through the mist, his voice scraped raw from three nights of shouting back at the dark.
Nelu [afraid]: Stay where I can see your faces, and do not say my name until we are sure of one another.
Nelu [weary]: They only come when the sun goes down, so I sleep by day and watch the water all night.
Nelu [weary]: Three nights I have sat here listening to them practice my mother's voice in the spray.
Nelu: The stone is too slick to climb with stiff fingers, even when the canyon goes quiet.
-> falls_day_menu

~ climb_day
Narrator: You knot the rope fast around a pine at the lip of the gorge and test your weight against the bark.
Narrator: Hand over hand, you go down the wet black rock with the cold spray of the falls beating into your face.
Narrator: The hemp holds, and your boots find the narrow ledge twenty feet below.
-> carried_day

~ climb_survival
Narrator: A careful eye picks out a seam of cracked black stone and the worn notches of an old goat path.
Narrator: Cold spray needles your faces as you work your way down from foothold to narrow foothold.
Narrator: The ledge is slick with moss, but it holds your weight when your boots touch down beside him.
-> carried_day

~ spell_day
Narrator: Magic pulls at the soles of your boots with a brief, weightless tug, as if the gorge has forgotten how to drop you.
Narrator: A heartbeat later, you stand on the wet stone ledge beside the boy.
-> carried_day

# Nelu comes up in the sun; the wisps are never met (xp fight pays what beating them would have).
~ carried_day
xp fight falls_wisps
set nelu_saved
quest called_by_name nelu_found
Narrator: You haul him up onto the wet grass at the lip of the gorge, where he sits shivering in the grey light.
Nelu [weary]: Up here in the sun, all that water sounds like nobody at all.
Nelu [sad]: If anything calls to me in the dark again, I am going to sing over it until my throat gives out.
Narrator: Below you, the gorge is only a gorge: black stone, white water, and cold mist rising.
Narrator: Nelu has not yet let go of the sleeve of the one who pulled him over the edge.
-> END
